# Generated demo artifacts (weights / pool / bootstrap / parity trajectory).
# Regenerable from the export pipeline (needs W&B access to the private project),
# deployed to the GitHub-Pages repo via `npm run deploy`. gallery.json (the small
# hand-maintained model registry) stays tracked.
public/weights/reverse_*.json
# Exception: the exact files gallery.json references (~1.8 MB total, byte-identical
# to what the live blog demo serves) are committed so a fresh clone can run the demo
# locally with no W&B access. Everything else under public/weights/ (parity
# trajectory for verify.html, superseded/experimental bundles) stays ignored.
!public/weights/reverse_fixed_no_damage.json
!public/weights/reverse_fixed_no_damage_demo.json
!public/weights/reverse_fixed_damage.json
!public/weights/reverse_fixed_damage_demo.json
!public/weights/reverse_random_damage_v33.json
